  "description": "LEXMIN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H92 O22 Y4,2(C4 H10 O1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.630-3.850 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.71-112.53°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Y4(μ3-OH)2(η2-accp)4((μ-O)-η2-accp)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
